- * @remarks The AI variants layer two gradients — a padding-box fill and a border-box stroke — for their frame, and `-color-ai-secondary` can't paint gradient text and a fill at once, so its centre stays transparent at rest and fills on hover or active. Ghost hover and active derive a low-opacity, slightly-darkened brand wash rather than using the raw hover-background tokens, which would print same-colour-on-same-colour text. Also sets its own icon/label `gap` and horizontal `padding`; chaining a `-gap-*`/`-p-*`/`-padding-*` spacing utility modifier overrides those built-in values.
+ * @remarks The AI variants layer two gradients — a padding-box fill and a border-box stroke — for their frame, and `-color-ai-secondary` can't paint gradient text and a fill at once, so its centre stays transparent at rest and fills on hover or active. `-without-background` hover and active derive a low-opacity, slightly-darkened brand wash rather than using the raw hover-background tokens, which would print same-colour-on-same-colour text. Also sets its own icon/label `gap` and horizontal `padding`; chaining a `-gap-*`/`-p-*`/`-padding-*` spacing utility modifier overrides those built-in values. The optional `.pfx-button-group` wrapper maps Figma's `.buttonGroup` and owns adjacent button spacing.
